      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Typical dosing is 400\u2013800 mg per dose, and 1600 mg is above the single-dose range as well. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg/day divided**, for example 800 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
